From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 09:19:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] drm/apple: Fix missing EDID on T6050 external displays

On the M5 Ultra Mac Studio (J775D) displays on the external display
processors had no EDID, so userspace failed to parse one and could not
identify the monitor. The connector's EDID is now built from the sink
metadata the firmware sends.

On firmware 27, T6050's external display processor serves its AV service
from another endpoint than earlier firmware does, while the driver binds
the AV service where earlier firmware has it. No service is announced
there, so the sink's EDID is never read and the connector has no EDID
property; userspace then fails to parse one.

Like the desktop 26.x external processor, it does send each sink's
DisplayAttributes and TimingElements. Set sink_metadata_edid for
apple,t6050-dcpext, so the connector's EDID is built from them on the
existing sink-metadata path, a new sink on each Type-C attachment.

This is the minimal firmware-27 EDID source. Reading the sink's own EDID
from the AV service where firmware 27 serves it, as dj's driver does, is
a planned follow-up.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from commit e59d1cf02526fd9c0e51026862011e00919eb072)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 964e1614ff98..fad745267532 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -554,9 +554,10 @@ void dcp_drm_crtc_page_flip(struct apple_dcp *dcp, ktime_t now)
 }
 
 /*
- * A desktop 26.x external processor does not hand out the sink's EDID through
- * its DCPAV service, but exports the TimingElements and DisplayAttributes
- * of every sink it drives, on HDMI and Type-C alike.
+ * A desktop 26.x external processor, and T6050's on firmware 27, does not
+ * hand out the sink's EDID through its DCPAV service, but exports the
+ * TimingElements and DisplayAttributes of every sink it drives, on HDMI and
+ * Type-C alike.
  */
 static bool dcp_sink_metadata(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 {
@@ -7052,6 +7053,7 @@ static const struct apple_dcp_hw_data apple_dcp_hw_t6050_dcpext = {
 	.num_dptx_ports = 2,
 	.adopt_live_session = true,
 	.firmware_compat = DCP_FIRMWARE_V_27_0,
+	.sink_metadata_edid = true,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id of_match[] = {
